# React Native + Expo — project rules

Source of truth: `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/*.md` and `docs/adr/`. Summary:

## Stack
Expo (development build) · React Compiler · TS strict · Expo Router · TanStack Query v5 · axios ·
i18next (en/es) · secure-store · StyleSheet + ui/theme.ts · expo-image · Jest/RNTL + network stubs · Maestro.
No store library, no DI, no repositories, no barrels, no zod, no generated API types, no persisted cache.

## Structure
- `src/app` routes are thin: read useAccount/useCapabilities/params, build links in core/hrefs.ts, render a feature screen.
- `src/core` (imports nothing above), `src/ui` (imports only ui), `src/features/<x>/{domain,data,presentation/{queries,components,screens},locales}`.
- Components never import `data/`. Features import each other only from account, employee, auth.
- Role decisions only in `features/account/capabilities.ts`.

## Data
- axios `api`/`publicApi`; failures are `ApiError` (`apiErrorOf`, `errorText`). 401 ends the session only if message is exactly `Unauthorized`.
- Raw types only with read fields; allow-list mapper per response + privacy contract test.
- `xxxKeys`, `xxxQueries` (queryOptions + CachePolicy), one-line hooks taking ids; GETs resent by the client only on 502/503/504; TanStack never retries; writes never resent.
- Use cases only for orchestration, in `domain/usecases/`, receiving fetchers as a parameter.

## Code style
- kebab-case files, named exports (except routes).
- Alphabetical: JSX props (key/ref first, on* last), object keys, type members, unions, named imports.
- Imports grouped: react/react-native → expo → third-party → `@/` → relative → `import type`.
- No `console.*` (core/monitoring only), no `any`, no hex/magic numbers (theme tokens), no hardcoded text (en + es).
- No `try` in .tsx or use* hooks. Files ≤250 lines target, 450 max.
- Never edit `ios/`, `android/`. Add deps with `npx expo install`.

## Tests
Next to code; fixtures in `*.fixture.ts`; privacy contract test per mapper; every logic fix with a regression test.
